title: 'xcm-builder: add TeleportAndBurnForwarderForAccountId32'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `TeleportAndBurnForwarderForAccountId32`, a `pallet_accumulate_and_forward::Forwarder`
    that teleports native tokens to a destination chain and burns them there with `BurnAsset`.
    It is meant for networks without a DAP whose issuance is tracked on Asset Hub, such as the
    Kusama system chains, which currently carry their own copy of this logic.
    `TeleportForwarderForAccountId32` keeps its behaviour; both forwarders now share the local
    execution and rollback logic.

    Integration note: the origin is preserved, so the destination receives
    `AliasOrigin(source chain/AccountId32(account))`, `UnpaidExecution`, `BurnAsset` and its
    barrier checks the aliased location. Before switching to this forwarder, the destination
    (e.g. Asset Hub Kusama) must allow unpaid execution for the accumulation accounts, as Asset
    Hub Polkadot does with `SystemChainAccumulationAccounts`. Otherwise the source chain removes
    the tokens, the destination rejects the message, and the destination issuance drifts.
crates:
- name: staging-xcm-builder
  bump: minor
